<http://data.silknow.org/object/51d6ada3-8284-32da-a5c7-ea601d5fc21c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Robe for a No dancer of brocaded silk and satin. The upper part is woven in silk and gilt paper strips on a satin ground. The skirts are woven in gold thread on a silk ground. Made up of several pieces stitched together, it is cut square, and has short square sleeves, slightly rounded off at the lower ends. Between the skirts is a long narrow opening. Pattern on the upper part consists of a diaper of rosettes within hexagons. Lined with silk."@en , "Robe of brocaded silk satin, woven in gilt paper strips, silk and gold thread, Japan, 19th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/076de939-105f-3c58-8405-9ce3b0afefd1> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Robe for a No dancer of brocaded silk and satin. The upper part is woven in silk and gilt paper strips on a satin ground. The skirts are woven in gold thread on a silk ground. Made up of several pieces stitched together, it is cut square, and has short square sleeves, slightly rounded off at the lower ends. Between the skirts is a long narrow opening. Pattern on the upper part consists of a diaper of rosettes within hexagons. Lined with silk."@en , "Robe of brocaded silk satin, woven in gilt paper strips, silk and gold thread, Japan, 19th century"@en ;
